### Goal Model Decomposition

#### Goals

| Name | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Target Condition | Relation | Justification |
|------|------|---------|-----------|------------------|----------|---------------|
| G1 | Deliver Resources | - | Achieve | All resources are delivered to the specified location | - | The mission's objective is to ensure resources are delivered. |
| G2 | Collect Resources | - | Perform | Resources are collected from storage | AND | Collection is necessary before delivery. |
| G3 | Deliver Resources | - | Achieve | All resources are delivered to the specified location | AND | Delivery is the final objective after collection. |
| G2.1 | Retrieve Resources from Storage | - | Perform | Resources are retrieved from storage | AND | Essential step in the collection phase. |
| G2.2 | Recharge and Transfer Mission | - | Perform | Mission is transferred after recharging | FALLBACK | Fallback for low battery during collection. |
| G3.1 | Deliver Resources to Destination | - | Achieve | Resources are delivered to the specified location | AND | Final step in the delivery phase. |
| G3.2 | Return to Checkpoint and Transfer Mission | - | Perform | Mission is transferred after returning to checkpoint | FALLBACK | Fallback for low battery during delivery. |

#### Tasks

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| AT1 | Navigate to Storage | AND | Storage location | 1 | Single robot per storage. |
| AT2 | Send Request for Resources | AND | Storage location | 1 | Single action per storage. |
| AT3 | Wait for Resource Retrieval | AND | Storage location | 1 | Single action per storage. |
| AT4 | Navigate to Destination | AND | Destination location | 1 | Single delivery task. |
| AT5 | Deliver Resources | AND | Destination location | 1 | Single delivery task. |
| AT6 | Return to Checkpoint | AND | Checkpoint location | 1 | Fallback action for low battery. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Both collection and delivery are necessary for the mission.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [FALLBACK]**  
  Justification: If collection fails due to low battery, recharge and transfer.

- **G2.1 -> AT1, AT2, AT3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Sequential actions for retrieval.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [FALLBACK]**  
  Justification: If delivery fails due to low battery, return to checkpoint.

- **G3.1 -> AT4, AT5 [AND]**  
  Justification: Sequential delivery actions.

- **AT1, AT2, AT3 can be run in parallel**  
  Justification: Multiple storages can be handled by multiple robots.

This model ensures that the mission is decomposed into manageable goals and tasks, with fallbacks for battery issues and parallel execution for efficiency.
